  "semantic_description": {
    "level_1_elemental": "Histogram of API gateway response latency. Value axis (x) is request latency in milliseconds on a base-10 log scale spanning ~10 ms to ~5,000 ms, binned into ~24 log-width bins; the y axis is the count of requests per bin, zero-baselined.",
    "level_2_statistical": "Strongly right-skewed, unimodal distribution. The mode and median sit near 80\u2013100 ms (p50 \u2248 82 ms); the bulk of mass falls between 30 and 200 ms. A long thin tail extends past 1 s, with p95 \u2248 600 ms and p99 \u2248 2.3 s; the slowest requests reach ~4.8 s.",
    "level_3_perceptual": "A dense body cluster in the low-hundreds-of-ms collapses smoothly into a thinning high-latency tail on the log axis \u2014 there is no second bump, so the slow requests are a continuous tail rather than a distinct bimodal slow cohort. On a linear axis this tail would be invisibly compressed against the right edge.",
    "level_4_contextual": null,
    "short_alt": "Log-x histogram of 48,210 API latencies, where most cluster near 82 ms but a long tail runs past 2 seconds.",
